  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe shipped sinker post can post Sinker Side Burn with explicit machine data.\nThe machine must state `edm.codes.side` with `{x}`, `{y}`, `{z}`, and `{f}`.\nThe machine editor exposes this optional code role.\nThe post fills absolute endpoints in the work offset and converts coordinates and feed to the document units.\nThe downward entry still uses `edm.codes.depth`.\nEach lateral feed uses the machine's `side` template.\nThe post refuses incomplete templates, incomplete coordinates, diagonal travel, changing lateral Z, invalid feed, and travel below program resolution.\nStraight burns still need no lateral code.\n\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/3001-sinker-side-burn.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe post refused every Side Burn before the section opened.\nIts feed handler supported downward Z burns only.\nThe generated Side Burn already states the plunge, lateral feed, return feed, and rapid retract.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe first pin failed on unchanged production code at `f8a554045`.\nIt failed with the existing named Side Burn refusal.\nThe failure text remains outside the branch at `/tmp/3001-red.txt`.\n\nThe `script_sinker_side` suite passes all ten pins:\n\n- `recorded_side_burn_posts_both_lateral_legs`\n- `lateral_direction_and_amount_follow_each_recorded_axis`\n- `lateral_endpoint_feed_and_electrode_reference_use_document_units_and_wcs`\n- `straight_and_side_burns_post_together_to_recorded_nc`\n- `side_burn_requires_explicit_complete_machine_dialect`\n- `side_burn_refuses_diagonal_and_combined_vertical_lateral_moves`\n- `side_burn_refuses_missing_or_non_numeric_start_and_end_coordinates`\n- `side_burn_refuses_missing_zero_or_negative_feed`\n- `side_burn_refuses_motion_below_the_program_resolution`\n- `side_dialect_does_not_enable_lateral_moves_in_a_straight_burn`\n\nThe existing `script_sinker_iso` suite passes all 22 tests.\nIts missing-dialect pin still refuses a Side Burn before any burn code.\nThe straight burn keeps its existing golden output.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Copy the original post from `upstream/main` back over the fixed script | Nine new pins fail. All ten pass after restoration. |\n| Remove the required-placeholder guard | The complete-machine-dialect pin fails, then passes after restoration. |\n| Remove the complete-coordinate guard | The missing-coordinate pin fails, then passes after restoration. |\n| Remove the axis and constant-Z guard | The diagonal and combined-travel pin fails, then passes after restoration. |\n| Remove the positive-feed guard | The invalid-feed pin fails, then passes after restoration. |\n| Remove the formatted-zero-feed guard | The invalid-feed pin fails, then passes after restoration. |\n| Remove the endpoint-resolution guard | The program-resolution pin fails, then passes after restoration. |\n\n## Machine editor screenshots\n\nThe optional `Code side` row exposes the lateral burn template.\nBefore this change, the row is absent.\nThe screenshots show the same synthetic sinker machine in the real editor.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Sinker machine editor before the Code side row](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d3df7752dd87941ffe373f13dea9103edcb77db6/3027/machine-editor-before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![Sinker machine editor with the optional Code side row](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d3df7752dd87941ffe373f13dea9103edcb77db6/3027/machine-editor-after.png)\n\n## Review validation\n\nThe validation base is `upstream/main` at `768fe23f0205359323bd7dd723700c95c57eee89`.\n\nThe current `Milling-test.step` fixture imports as 6,228 facets.\nThe Linux bore pin now expects `(3158, 3130, 1141)`.\nThe pin also checks the mesh size and planar cuts at Z = 0, 5, 10, and 15 mm.\nThe warning, fallback, and time-budget checks remain.\n\nThe existing machine editor structural test checks `Code side` by its literal label.\nThis check does not depend on the production code-role list.\n\nThe UI pin mutation removes `side` from the production code-role list.\n`the_sinker_section_shows_keys_orbits_conditions_and_codes_with_not_stated` then fails at the literal `Code side` assertion.\nIt passes after restoration: one test passed, exit 0.\n\nBore mutations:\n\n- Restore the old Linux path tuple: the exact heavy test fails with `(3158, 3130, 1141)`.\n- Remove one imported facet: the mesh pin fails with 6,227 instead of 6,228 facets.\n- Change stepdown to 10 mm: the level pin fails with `[0, 10]` instead of `[0, 5, 10, 15]`.\n\nAll mutation edits were restored.\nThe fixed heavy test passes: one test passed in 2.09 seconds.\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --only \"app heavy: pocket3d_hsm\"` passes.\nThe final targeted heavy check has one step and one passed test, with no failed or ignored tests.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes: 126 steps and 2,291 passed tests.\nNo test fails. Nine tests are ignored by the existing lane rules: two bore heavy or known-fail tests and seven UI tests.\nThe UI library runs 1,318 tests successfully.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nOne new file: `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/sinker-iso/sinker_side_burn.nc`.\nThe full diff was inspected.\nIts 24 lines contain a straight burn, then a Side Burn plunge and both 0.15 mm lateral legs.\nThe lateral blocks use invented test codes from the synthetic dialect.\nNo existing NC or CL golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo real EDM control or physical cut was exercised.\nNo real machine dialect was added.\nThe tests post the existing recorded CL fixtures through the shipped script.\nThe complete catalog workflow and manual machine editor interaction were not exercised.\nThe screenshots render the actual editor with a synthetic fixture through the test harness.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2893 touches `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` in the drilling cycle rows. This PR changes the sinker row.\n- #2554 touches `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` in the `controller.post` section. This PR changes the EDM code roles.\n\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nNeither changes the same lines or post functions.\nNo stack is required.\n\nEffort: high\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: Sinker Side Burn posts explicit lateral feeds when the machine states a complete lateral servo template, with named refusals for unsupported data and unsafe moves.\n\nFixes #3001\n",
